{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773943323,"nonce":"bzZO8spapXBoxTv4Qqhy1TexNro=","title":"P4: Fork/resume flows, auto-fork policy, SDK resume threading","message":"Wire fork/resume actions end-to-end, add auto-fork policy setting, thread resume params to SDK.\n\nParent: 86b63bc\nDepends on: 40f0298 (P2 — API endpoints), a0963df (P3 — UI action buttons)\n\n## Fork flow\n- \"Fork from here\" action in message action bar → POST /api/conversations/:id/fork\n- On success: navigate to the new conversation in History tab (#/chat-history?conv=\u003cnew_id\u003e)\n- Show toast: \"Forked conversation up to this message\"\n\n## Resume flow\n- \"Resume from here\" action in message action bar → POST /api/conversations/:id/resume\n- On success: navigate to Console tab (#/console?session=\u003cnew_session_id\u003e)\n- Show toast: \"Resumed conversation in Console\"\n\n## Auto-fork policy\n- New setting in Mandible settings: resume_conflict_policy = \"auto_fork\" | \"prompt\" | \"allow_concurrent\"\n- Default: \"auto_fork\"\n- Before creating a resume Console session, check if any existing Console session has the same provider_session_id\n- If conflict detected:\n  - auto_fork: silently fork, then resume the fork. Toast: \"Conversation active elsewhere — forked to new session\"\n  - prompt: show dialog with Branch (resume in-place) vs Fork options, with \"Remember my choice\" checkbox\n  - allow_concurrent: just resume (power user, risk of interleaving)\n- Add to settings UI (settings.tsx) and settings API\n\n## SDK backend changes\n- ConsoleSession type (src/types.ts): add resume_at_message?: string\n- SDKBackend.buildQueryOptions(): when this.meta.resume_at_message is set AND this is the first prompt, pass resume: this.meta.provider_session_id and resumeSessionAt: this.meta.resume_at_message to sdk.query() options\n- After the first prompt, clear resume_at_message (subsequent prompts continue normally)\n- PTY backend: when resume_at_message is set, add --resume \u003cprovider_session_id\u003e to launch args (already partially implemented)\n\n## UI wiring\n- History tab (conversations.tsx): wire message action bar fork/resume buttons to API calls\n- Console tab: the new Console session created by resume should pre-hydrate from conversation history (the existing history-first hydration handles this automatically via provider_session_id)\n- App.tsx: add handleConversationFork and handleConversationResume handlers, thread through to views","files":null}]}